WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.580
Every major project begins with ambition.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:08.250
Turning that ambition into a
controlled, financeable and deliverable
outcome requires more than information.

3
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.010
Project professionals must connect scope,
schedule, cost, finance, risk and performance

4
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.350
while making accountable decisions in
increasingly complex environments.

5
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.590
Artificial intelligence can accelerate
analysis, identify patterns, compare
scenarios and support forecasting.

6
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.650
But a convincing AI output is not
automatically a reliable project decision.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.090
Responsible adoption requires verified data,
transparent assumptions, meaningful human review,

8
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.050
clear decision rights and an evidence trail
that can withstand professional challenge.

9
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.300
PCI AI — Project Controls Institute Global
— focuses on the professional competence

10
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.150
needed to govern AI-supported work across project
controls, project finance and project management.

11
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.990
Its professional credential framework
includes PCL-AI for project controls,

12
00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.350
PFL-AI for project finance and
PML-AI for project management.

13
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:02.670
The future of project delivery will
not be defined by technology alone.

14
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:10.550
It will be shaped by professionals who
know when to trust, when to challenge
and how to remain accountable.

15
00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:14.750
Discover PCI AI at pciai.org

